cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference this simulation study, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: "Research Project"
    given-names: "Computational Battery Lab"
title: "Physics-informed estimation of lithium-ion battery state of charge and degradation under elevated ambient temperatures"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-29
url: "https://github.com/warlord80/battery-bms-temperature-project"
abstract: >-
  This computational study develops a reduced-order electrothermal and
  aging-aware equivalent-circuit model for controlled sensitivity analysis of
  lithium-ion battery state-of-charge estimation under elevated ambient
  temperatures and capacity degradation.
keywords:
  - lithium-ion battery
  - state of charge
  - equivalent circuit model
  - extended kalman filter
  - battery thermal modeling
  - electrothermal simulation
license: MIT
